    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "AMERICA'S\nGREATEST\nAIRPORT\nAN FRANCISCO harbor was\nonce, scientists tell us, a\nplacid lake lying in a valley.\nThen the earth heaved and\nthe ocean crashed through\nGolden Gate — making the\ngreatest natural harbor in the western\nhemisphere.\nToday this city— a metropolis be-\ncause of its magnificent harbor-plans\nto enlarge its airport to one that will\ncompare with the famous airfields of\nCroyden, England, and Tempelhof,\nGermany\n-unapproached at present\nby any in America.\nCovering more than 1,000 acres,\npierced by an arterial highway twenty\nminutes from the city's center and\nflanked on three sides by the Bay of\nSan Francisco, Mills Field presents an\nideal site.\n\"If Mills Field is not a good one,\"\nsaid Col. Lindbergh,\n\"we all should\nquit flying.\"\nAnd his unqualified ad\nmiration has been confirmed by Gen-\neral Gilmore, Col. Brant, Commander\nKingsford-Smith and other\nflyers of a national and in-\nternational fame.\nWith but a fraction of\nits field completed San\nFrancisco's Municipal Air-\nport already enjoys the\ndistinction of staging the\nlargest army maneuvers\noutside of\na government\nstation and when com\npleted more than 2,000\nairplanes, amphibians and\nseaplanes can be parked\nthere.\nOF SAN\nFRANCISCO\nAY\nBAYSHORE\nBIEN\n20 MINUTES\nSan Francisco's\nCivic Center\nSAN FRANCISCO\nMUNICIPAL\nAIRPORT\nProposed Plan for Additions\nand Improvements to\nMILLS FIELD",
      "Mills\nFialo\nSAN FRANCISCO\nMUNICIPAL AIRPORT\nTo BE America's first two-unit operated\nairport, simplifying traffic rules and allowing\nfor the landing and take-off of 2,000 planes.\nCovers more than 1,100 acres.\nIncludes 500 acres restricted area for airplane\nindustries.\nNo flying hazards: free from congested area;\nSan Francisco Bay on three sides allowing\nfor yacht harbor.\nInty minutes from city's center on arterial\nhighway.\nPassed by all north and south bus routes.\nAdjacent to Southern Pacific and Western\nPacific Railroads.\nIdeal water landings for amphibians and sea-\nplanes.\nIdeal year-round climatical and visibility con-\nditions allowing entry and exit practically\nevery day in the year.\nGood buoyancy and lift practically assured\nat all times by prevailing northwest trade\nwinds.\nCost of proposed improvements $4,000,000.\nTHE PLANNERS OF\nAMERICA'S GREATEST\nAIRPORT\nHON. E. J. SPAULDING\nChairman\nHON. CARL W. MILES\nHON. JEFFERSON E. PEYSER\nCAPT. ROY N. FRANCIS\nSuperintendent\nAlready with\nAmerica's\nGreatest SEA\nPORT.\nSAN\nFRANCISCO\nNow Plans\nThe world's\ngreatest\nAIRPORT\nMILLS FIELD\nCovering more than\n1100 ACRES\non Bayshore Boulevard"
    ],
